  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n### Description\n\nI’m experimenting with the `interestfor` attribute together with the Popover API, and I’m seeing behavior that seems inconsistent or unclear.\n\n---\n\n### Issue 1: `hide` actions are not respected\n\nWhen using:\n\n* `popovertargetaction=\"hide\"`\n* or `command=\"hide-popover\"`\n\n…the popover does not stay hidden as expected.\n\nInstead, if the trigger element has `interestfor`, the popover reappears immediately on hover, even after explicitly hiding it.\n\n---\n\n### Example\n\n```html\n<button interestfor=\"test\" popovertargetaction=\"hide\">Hide popover</button>\n\n<div id=\"test\" popover>\n  Some helpful info\n</div>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Observed behavior\n\n* Moving the mouse over the trigger (`?`) immediately shows it again\n* This makes `hide` actions feel ineffective\n\n---\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n* When explicitly hidden via a user action, the popover should remain hidden\n\n---\n\n### Issue 2: Lack of control over interaction type\n\nCurrently, `interestfor` seems to implicitly trigger on hover (and possibly focus), but:\n\n* There is no way to restrict it to:\n\n  * hover only\n  * click only\n  * focus only\n\n---\n\n### Question\n\nIs there (or will there be) a way to control how `interestfor` is triggered?\n\nFor example:\n\n```html\n<button interestfor=\"hint\" interesttrigger=\"click\">\n```\n\nor\n\n```html\n<button interestfor=\"hint\" interesttrigger=\"hover\">\n```\n\n---\n\n### Additional context\n\n* Combining:\n\n  * `interestfor`\n  * manual hide actions\n\ncreates conflicting behavior between:\n\n* automatic showing (via interest)\n* manual dismissal (via popover controls)\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n1. `hide` actions (`popovertargetaction=\"hide\"` / `hide-popover`) are not respected when `interestfor` is present\n2. There is currently no way to control the trigger mechanism (hover vs click vs focus)\n\n---\n\n### Questions for maintainers\n\n* Is this the intended behavior of `interestfor`?\n* Are there plans to support configurable triggers?\n* How should developers properly handle dismissal when using `interestfor`?\n\n---\n\nThanks!\n",
